Inclusions: impairments of ideational perseveration, tangentiality and circumstantiality</ns4:description>
    <rdfs:label>Form of thought</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.stiima.cnr.it/ICF-exc-coreset#d355">
    <ns4:description xml:lang="en">Starting, sustaining and ending an examination of a matter, with arguments for or against, or debate carried out by means of spoken, written, sign or other forms of language, with one or more people one knows or who are strangers, in formal or casual settings.

Inclusions: discussion with one person or many people</ns4:description>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.stiima.cnr.it/ICF-exc-coreset#d355"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <ns4:nomeIta>Discussione</ns4:nomeIta>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.stiima.cnr.it/RientraOnt3Merged#Hearing_Loss"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.stiima.cnr.it/ICF-exc-coreset#Activities_and_participation"/>
    <ns4:descrizioneITA>Avviare, mantenere e terminare lâ€™esame di una questione, fornendo argomenti a favore o contro, o un dibattito realizzato attraverso linguaggio verbale, scritto, dei segni o altre forme di linguaggio, con una o piÃ¹ persone conosciute o meno, in contesti formali o informali.

Inclusione: discussione con una o molte persone</ns4:descrizioneITA>
    <rdfs:label>Discussion</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
